    "created_at": "2023-09-26T08:11:37Z",
    "updated_at": "2023-09-26T08:11:58Z",
    "body": "> > Also, it could make sense to use the parameterize fixture\r\n> \r\n> What do you mean with parameterize fixture?\r\n\r\nYou can define resuable fixtures (e.g. instances of classes) that can be called in the tests without redefining it in every test. If you want one test to apply to multiple fixutres, you can parametrize them in a decorator. You can look at the [qsvc tests](https://github.com/sQUlearn/squlearn/blob/main/tests/kernel/ml/test_qsvc.py) as examples. Here, projected and fidelity instances are defined as fixtures which are then called with the parametrized \"qsvc\" variable, e.g. in test_predict (line 80)",
    "author_association": "COLLABORATOR",
